UID:2bd525302f6f73c4@delhi-events
DTSTAMP:20260920T105600Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260909
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261223
SUMMARY:Inheritors of Earth
LOCATION:KNMA\, New Delhi\, Kiran Nadar Museum of Art\, Saket\, New Delhi
  110017
URL:https://www.knma.org/whats-on/exhibitions/inheritors-of-earth
DESCRIPTION:Inheritors of Earth \, curated by Premjish Achari\, invites v
 iewers into the relational world of plants\, entities long treated as bac
 kdrop\, resource\, or specimen rather than co-inhabitants of the earth. T
 he title draws on Vaikom Muhammad Basheer’s Bhumiyude Avakashikal \, en
 visioning humans\, flora and fauna as equal co-custodians of the planet\,
  and on ecological activist Kallen Pokkudan\, whose mangrove-planting wor
 k fused Dalit history with ecological repair. Through paintings\, photogr
 aphs\, installations and video\, artists here practice a “phytosensitiv
 e” approach: encountering rather than merely representing plants\, trac
 ing colonial botanical migrations\, and honoring uncredited lower-caste k
 nowledge-keepers erased from scientific archives. Rejecting both extracti
 on and exoticism\, the exhibition asks viewers to look with plants\, not 
 just at them\, moving from usefulness and utility toward humility\, kinsh
 ip\, and coexistence—imagining a future shaped by plant life on its own
  terms. The exhibition is proud to host a set of artworks from the Shared
  Ecologies archive as part of an extended reading room. Ben Goldfarb has 
 designed a special soundscape for the exhibition. Independent curator and
  researcher Oorja Garg and IMPULSE Magazine\, New York are leading a spec
 ial reading group for the duration of the exhibition.\n\nhttps://www.knma
 .org/whats-on/exhibitions/inheritors-of-earth
CATEGORIES:exhibition\,art\,history\,nature\,sociology
END:VEVENT
